The privileged helper is a LocalSystem Windows service that performs ONLY
host network standup (New-VMSwitch / New-NetNat / New-NetIPAddress) on behalf of
non-elevated builds, over a named pipe ACL'd to Administrators and Hyper-V
Administrators. With it installed, 'warden build --driver hyperv' runs entirely
without elevation and stands up a fresh isolated network per build (no shared
durable switch). VM lifecycle always runs in-process; only network standup is
delegated.

Usage:
  warden hyperv service [command]

Available Commands:
  install     Install and start the privileged helper service (run once, elevated)
  run         Run the privileged helper (invoked by the SCM; or in a console to smoke-test)
  uninstall   Stop and remove the privileged helper service (elevated)

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for service

Global Flags:
      --color string     color output (auto, always, never)
      --config string    config file to read, the only one that is (default: WARDEN_CONFIG, then ./warden.toml if it exists)
      --driver string    orchestration driver (container, qemu, vz, hyperv, firecracker)
      --runtime string   container runtime (finch, docker, podman)
  -v, --verbose          verbose output

Use "warden hyperv service [command] --help" for more information about a command.
